g__bob-cli","clan_summary":"[bold #D75FFF]◆ EPIC bob-cli-5y[/bold #D75FFF]\n[dim]  Title: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]Ref tasks live with the work they serve[/bold #D7AFFF]\n[dim]   Goal: [#D7D7AF][/dim]Every open reference has exactly one ordinary reading task, `#task [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]#ref` with a unique `^ref-<slug>` block ID, in the `## Tasks` [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]section of a real area, project, or inbox note, and that note is [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]the reference's parent. Capture paths ask for, or receive, the [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]parent. A done/-aware locator keeps ref-note status in sync [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]wherever the task moves or is archived. The `#hide` and residence [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]special cases are gone, and the 29 open refs are migrated without [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]losing a field, link, or dependency.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim] Counts: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]14[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] phases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]7[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plan:202610/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]ref_tasks_live_with_parent.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202610/ref_tasks_live_with_parent.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]bob-cli-5y[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/bobs-org/bob-cli--beads/blob/main/pages/bob-cli-5y/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]sase: file hooks export SASE_FILE_HOOK_PROJECT[/bold #D7AFFF]                [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]sase-hook-env[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]sase-hook-env: the sase file-hook runner exports the producing project's[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]name to every hook command as an environment variable, with docs and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]dispatch tests.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]One strict parent resolver and project_name_aliases[/bold #D7AFFF]           [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]parent-resolver[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]parent-resolver: add the shared area/project/inbox resolver with [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]project_name_aliases, expose aliases in capture-targets, and resolve an [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]explicit bob ref create -P.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Freshness keys refs on the #ref tag, with the lane split[/bold #D7AFFF]      [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]freshness-rekey[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]freshness-rekey: re-key ref review identity from the ^ref block ID to [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the #ref tag in Rust and bob-ledger-tools; Ready refs keep REFERENCES [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]while Next/Pending refs walk their lanes.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Live alias, install, and the hook passes -P[/bold #D7AFFF]                   [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]hook-config[dim] · [dim][/dim]after sase-hook-env, parent-resolver[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]hook-config: install bob, add project_name_aliases to bob.md, confirm [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the live sase exports the variable, then switch the chezmoi hook command[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]to pass -P.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]The done/-aware ref-task locator and read-side contracts[/bold #D7AFFF]      [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n    [#AF87FF]ref-locator[dim] · [dim][/dim]after parent-resolver[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]ref-locator: build the read-only locator, derive status/parent/dates [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]from the located task, add the task object, diagnostics, ref list -P [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]aliases, and capture-complete task_kind.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  6 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]The open-book identity glyph and picker text[/bold #D7AFFF]                  [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]ref-glyph[dim] · [dim][/dim]after freshness-rekey[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]ref-glyph: specify and implement the #task #ref open-book glyph with [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]conformance vectors, and show reading tasks cleanly in plugin pickers.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  7 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Scan writes reading tasks into parent notes[/bold #D7AFFF]                   [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n    [#AF87FF]ref-sync-v2[dim] · [dim][/dim]after ref-locator[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]ref-sync-v2: births insert the v2 line into the parent's Tasks section, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]ref notes carry the managed embed, status syncs to the located line [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]across files, and annotation follow-ups go to the parent.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  8 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Bob Mac Capture reads located ref tasks[/bold #D7AFFF]                       [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]mac-refs-v2[dim] · [dim][/dim]after ref-locator[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]mac-refs-v2: decode the task object, join Today on path and block ID, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]refresh on root-note changes, and show the book symbol for ref tasks in [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]pickers and the inspector.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  9 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]bob ref create requires -P; ingest, jobs, and fallbacks carry [bold black on #FFD75F][/bold #D7AFFF] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]the parent[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]ref-create-parent[dim] · [dim][/dim]after hook-config, ref-sync-v2[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]ref-create-parent: make -P required with no default, thread the resolved[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]parent through typed ingest, ref jobs, and clip-failure fallbacks, and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]delete the obsidian_ref defaults.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  10 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Capture URL @route and gkeep pull choose the parent[/bold #D7AFFF]          [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n    [#AF87FF]capture-gkeep-parent[dim] · [dim][/dim]after ref-create-parent[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]capture-gkeep-parent: a bare URL plus one @route becomes a ref filed [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]there, previews and parse report the parent, and gkeep pull honors note [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]routes, -P, and a TTY prompt.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  11 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]bob ref migrate-tasks[/bold #D7AFFF]                                        [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n    [#AF87FF]migrate-tasks[dim] · [dim][/dim]after ref-sync-v2[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]migrate-tasks: add the dry-run-first, reversible command that moves open[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]v1 ref tasks into parent notes and rewrites every link and dependency ID[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]that pointed at them.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  12 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Bob Mac Capture asks where a captured link belongs[/bold #D7AFFF]           [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]mac-file-under[dim] · [dim][/dim]after capture-gkeep-parent, mac-refs-v2[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]mac-file-under: open a File under picker for a bare URL, insert the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]chosen @route, preview the destination, and match project_name_aliases.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  13 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Migrate the live vault[/bold #D7AFFF]                                       [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]live-migration[dim] · [dim][/dim]after hook-confi